<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Hardened Runtime entitlements for a Developer ID build.

  The Hardened Runtime is mandatory for notarization, and it denies a set of
  things by default. Only what Elemental actually needs is asked for here — an
  entitlement you do not need is an entitlement that widens the attack surface
  and that Apple may query at review.

  What is deliberately NOT here:

    * app sandbox. Elemental is distributed outside the App Store, and the
      sandbox would block it writing the screen saver's ByHost preferences and
      reading ~/Library/Application Support — the two channels the desktop uses
      to reach the saver. The screen saver itself runs inside Apple's own
      legacyScreenSaver.appex sandbox regardless of what we ask for.

    * com.apple.security.device.camera / microphone / addressbook and friends.
      Nothing here touches them.

    * JIT, unsigned executable memory, DYLD variables. Metal compiles the shader
      at runtime from an embedded string, which uses the system Metal compiler
      service and needs none of these. If a future change makes the shader fail
      to build ONLY in a signed build, this is the first place to look — but do
      not add them speculatively.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Where the sky is drawn for. Without this the app falls back to the
         configured or estimated place, which is a degraded but working scene —
         see Config.fallbackPlace. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.location</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Open-Meteo, METAR and the RainViewer radar composite. All outbound;
         nothing listens. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
